# Build artifacts
build/
.build/
*.o
*.ll
*.bc
*.s

# A package's marker: `rz pack` writes it into a staged tree only
# (docs/PACKAGES.md §2); one in a checkout would make it a package.
ritz-package.toml

# Incremental compile caches (cache.py: .ritz-cache[-<compiler>]/), anywhere
.ritz-cache*/

# Task-room worktrees (spawned agent rooms live here)
.claude/worktrees/

# Temp dirs (repo root and cryptosec compile temps)
/tmp*/
projects/cryptosec/tmp*/

# Compiled project binaries (reproducible via make build)
projects/nexus/nexus
projects/zeus/zeus
projects/zeus/test_client
projects/zeus/echo_worker
projects/tome/tome-cli
projects/tome/tome-server
# bench members: built by `rz build --all` since it reads rz.toml members (#1345)
bench/regressions/2026-05-04/s2_module_init/s2_module_init
bench/regressions/2026-05-04/s3_param_shadow/s3_param_shadow
projects/tome/run-tests
projects/goliath/goliath-tests
projects/goliath/goliath
projects/rzrz/rzrz
projects/lexis/lexis
projects/tempest/tempest
projects/tempest/tempest-tab

# Incremental-compilation cache (per-function token hash + cached LLVM IR).
# These are build artifacts — regenerated on every compile. Never commit.
*.ritz.sig

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Editor/IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store

# Logs
logs/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak

# Core dumps (never commit these — one slipped into mausoleum before,
# removed in Phase II-E cleanup).  Dump names only: `core`, `core.<pid>`.
# Never `core.*`: it hid smoke_stack/core.py from #3455's commit (AGAST
# #3559).  `!core/` keeps a directory named core (a package) visible.
core
core.[0-9]*
!core/

# Agent migration docs (temporary)
MIGRATION_INSTRUCTIONS.md
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Machine-local room permissions, written by .claude/provision-room.sh.
# Contains this host's permission grants for a headless agent; it is per-worktree
# state, not project configuration, and must never be committed from a task room.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Convenience symlinks placed at each project root by build.py, pointing
# into the (already-ignored) build/debug/ tree. They are regenerated by any
# build and resolve to nothing on a fresh clone, so committing them would
# publish broken links. 34 of these were staged by a blanket `git add` on
# 2026-09-12 and caught before landing.
